; -*- LISP -*-
;
; This is an input file for flac, not a LISP source code.
; But it is displayed in LISP mode to distinguish the comments.
;
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
; Simple ocean-ocean subduction
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
;
;==================================================================
;             M e s h    P a r a m e t e r s 
;==================================================================
333 167            number of _elements_ in X and Z directions: (nx-1),(nz-1)
0.e+3,0.e+3           x0,z0 begin.coord
250.e+3,-125.e+3    rxbo,rzbo (size of the region, rxbo > 0, rzbo < 0)
;
0, points.xy    ircoord, coordfile: read init. coordinates from the file
;
; X direction
0     Number zones X-direction (0 - regular grid)
; nelem per zone    size(non-dimen, must sum to 1.0)
;50  0.33
;200  0.34
;50  0.33
;
; Z direction
0                Number zones Z-direction (0 - regular grid)
; nelem per zone    size(non-dimen, must sum to 1.0)
;100  0.34
;50   0.66
; 
;
;===================================================================
;        C o n d i t i o n s:  M e c h a n i c a l
;===================================================================
; nystressbc, nydrsides
; Stress boundary conditions (0:no,1:yes), lithostatic stress bc on the sides (0/1)
1  1 
; nofbc: Number of boundary conditions
2
;----------------------------------------------------------------
;nofside       1-left,2-bottom,3-right,4-top,5-mid-plate
;nbc1,nbc2     range of application of boundary condition
;nbc           type of boundary condition
;  there are the following forms of boundary conditions:
;  0  - no conditions
;  10 - velx            01 - velz
;  20 - normal stress   02 - shear stress (x,z) plane
;  30 - vely                (strike slip version)
;----------------------------------------------------------------
;  Function of boundary conditions:
;------------------------------------------------------------------
;f = a + bx + cx**2 + (d cos (2pi ex) + f sin (2pi gx))*exp((x-i)*h)^2
;Dependence on time:   f(time) = f*(1 + df1*nstep) + df2*nstep
;------------------------------------------------------------------
;where x is undimensional. i.e. x = (x - x(na1)) / (x(na2) - x(na1))
;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;nofside  nbc1 nbc2  nbc   a       b    c     d     e     f      g     h     i 
1         1   168    10   -1.6e-10   0. 0.    0.    0.    0.     0.    0.    0.
3         1    168    10    1.6e-10   0. 0.    0.    0.    0.     0.    0.    0.
;
; Hydrostatic pressure  applied at the bottom (on the depth of rzbo and TOP!!)
; {y,n(1,0),auto(2)}, Pressure at compens.depth, substratum phase, addit. dens. diff, damp_vis
2                   0.                       8            0.            0.e+7
;
; Gravity
9.81
;=============================================================
;            C o n d i t i o n s : T h e r m a l
;=============================================================
0       -iprestress (fix boundaries) topo build up  stress up buyoancy are there for 200000. yrs
1        - itherm  (1-mech+therm, 2-no mech)
1        - if_hydro  (1-hydrothermal circulatio, 0-no hydro )
0        - istress_therm: Add THERMAL STRESSES (0,1,2-just 1 step)
0        - ishearh: Add SHEAR heating
1        - isolidus: chose a solidus (1-Katz (default),2-Hirschmann, 3-Herzberg, 4-McKenzie & Bickle).
10.       - t_top (Surface temperature in Celsius). Boundary AND initial condition.
1330.     - t_bot (Bottom temperature in Celsius). ONLY initial condition.
;
; Radiogenic heating
1.e-9, 10.      - hs (W/kg ~ 1.e-9),  hr (radio_fold) (km)
;
; Bottom Boundary conditions flag and value (1- temperature, 2- heat flux in mW/m2, 3 - asth. pot. temp) 
3 1450. 
;
; Predefined distributions
0              irtemp (0,1) (read temperature file or not)
proftemp.dat   temperature profile dat.file
;
; If (iynts = 2) Initially Variable thermal age continental and oceanic lithosphere accross the box (for convenience cont crust iph=1,
; oceanic crust iph = 2, oceanic mantle (dry) iph = 3, continental mantle (wet weak) iph = 4)
1              - nzone_age (number of zones of different age max 20)
;ictherm, age (Myr.), tp1, tp2, nph_layer (N), x nodes 1 and 2
;    nph_layer (N), layer depth #1 (km), #2, ..., #N-1
;    layer phase #1, #2, ..., #N
12, 100., 120, 15, 1, 334
     3,   30, 86
     2,    4,  8
;
;===================================================================
;                     R h e o l o g y
;===================================================================
; 1- elastic,
; 3- visco-elastic (Maxwell,Non-Newtonian) with softening
; 6- elasto-plastic (Mohr-Coulomb) with softening
;11- visco-elasto-plastic (Mohr-Coulomb,Fixed Maxwell,Newtonian) with softening
;12- visco-elasto-plastic (Mohr-Coulomb,Maxwell,Non-Newtonian) with softening
;
20  Number of Different Rheologies (<20)
;
;irheol,_,den, alfa,  beta,    n,       A,       E,    Lame:rl, Lame:rm,pls1,pls2,fric1,fric2, coh1, coh2,dilat1,dilat2,cond,    cp,     Ts,     Tl,     Tk, fk
;(1) basalt melt, 
12,1., 2900., 3.0e-5, 0.0e-11, 3.50, 1.10e+5, 4.30e+5, 4.3e+10, 4.3e+10, 0.0, 0.1, 30.0, 10.0, 4.e+7, 4.e+6,   0.0,   0.0, 3.3, 1000., 13000., 16000., 16000., 1.
;(2) continental crust, same as (6)
12,1., 2750., 3.0e-5, 0.0e-11, 3.05, 1.25e-1, 2.76e+5, 4.0e+10, 3.5e+10, 0.0, 0.1, 30.0, 20.0, 4.e+7, 4.e+6,   0.0,   0.0, 3.3, 1000., 13000., 16000., 16000., 1.
;(3) basalt (intruded in mantle), same as (7)
12,1., 2900., 3.0e-5, 0.0e-11, 3.05, 1.25e-1, 2.76e+5, 4.3e+10, 4.3e+10, 0.0, 0.1, 30.0, 30.0, 4.e+7, 4.e+6,   0.0,   0.0, 3.3, 1000., 13000., 16000., 16000., 1.
;(4) olivine, same as (8)
12,1., 3300., 3.0e-5, 0.0e-11, 3.50, 1.10e+5, 5.30e+5, 6.7e+10, 6.7e+10, 0.0, 5., 30.0, 30.0, 4.e+7, 4.e+6,   0.0,   0.0, 3.3, 1000., 13000., 16000., 16000., 1.
;(5) shist, transformed from (17)
11,1., 2900., 3.0e-5, 0.0e-12, 3.00, 7.00e+4, 3.76e+5, 3.0e+10, 3.0e+10, 0.0, 0.1, 30.0, 15.0, 4.e+7, 4.e+6,   0,     0,  3.3, 1000., 13000., 16000., 16000., 1.
;(6) continental crust, same as (2)
12,1., 2750., 3.0e-5, 0.0e-11, 3.05, 1.25e-1, 2.76e+5, 4.0e+10, 3.5e+10, 0.0, 0.1, 30.0, 15.0, 4.e+7, 4.e+6,   0.0,   0.0, 3.3, 1000., 13000., 16000., 16000., 1.
;(7) basalt (extrustives), same as (3)
12,1., 2900., 3.0e-5, 0.0e-11, 3.05, 1.25e-1, 2.76e+5, 4.3e+10, 4.3e+10, 0.0, 0.1, 30.0, 5.0, 44.e+6, 4.e+6,   0.0,   0.0, 3.3, 1000., 13000., 16000., 16000., 1.
;(8) olivine, same as (4), transformed from (9)
12,1., 3300., 3.0e-5, 0.0e-11, 3.50, 1.1e+5 5.30e+5, 6.7e+10, 6.7e+10, 0.0, 5., 30.0, 30.0, 4.e+7, 4.e+6,   0.0,   0.0, 3.3, 1000., 13000., 16000., 16000., 1.
;(9) weak olivine (serpentinized peridotite), transformed from (4) and (8), if overlying subducted oceaninc crust phase (3), (7) or (11); transform back to (4) if deeper than 65 km
12,1., 3000., 3.0e-5, 0.0e-11, 3.00, 7.00e+4, 1.20e+5, 5.0e+10, 3.0e+10, 0.0, 0.1,  15.0,  15.0, 4.e+6, 4.e+6,   0.0,   0.0, 3.3, 1000., 13000., 16000., 16000., 1.
;(10) sediment 2, not used
12,1., 2500., 3.0e-5, 0.0e-11, 3.00, 5.00e2 , 2.00e+5, 3.0e+10, 3.0e+10, 0.0, 0.1,  5.0,  1.0, 4.e+6, 4.e+6,   0.0,   0.0, 2.3, 1000., 13000., 16000., 16000., 1.
;(11) sediment 1, generated by erosion
12,1., 2650., 3.0e-5, 0.0e-11, 3.00, 5.00e2 , 3.00e+5, 3.0e+10, 3.0e+10, 0.0, 0.1,  10.0,  5.0, 4.e+6, 4.e+6,   0.0,   0.0, 2.3, 1000., 13000., 16000., 16000., 1.
;(12) weak crust, transformed from (2) and (6), if overlying oceanic crust (3), (7), (11), (14)
12,1., 2800., 3.0e-5, 0.0e-11, 3.00, 3.0e-6, 1.80e+5, 4.3e+10, 3.5e+10, 0.0, 0.1, 20.0,  20.0, 4.e+7, 4.e+6,   0.0,   0.0, 2.3, 1000., 13000., 16000., 16000., 1.
;(13) eclogite, transformed from (3) and (7), denser and more viscous
12,1., 3370., 3.0e-5, 0.0e-11, 3.05, 1.25e-1, 4.50e+5, 7.0e+10, 7.0e+10, 0.0, 0.1, 30.0, 30.0, 4.e+7, 4.e+6,   0.0,   0.0, 3.3, 1000., 13000., 16000., 16000., 1.
